 # Local
 $ eslint -f @microsoft/eslint-formatter-sarif . | reviewdog -f=sarif -diff="git diff"
 ````
+
+Before enabling a remote reporter, you can inspect the parsed paths and messages
+locally without posting comments:
+
+```shell
+reviewdog -f=sarif -reporter=rdjson -filter-mode=nofilter < report.sarif
+```
+
+For file-based reporting, check that each `physicalLocation.artifactLocation.uri`
+resolves to the intended file from the directory where reviewdog runs. An
+analysis identifier such as `analysis://run/123` is not a source-file location;
+keep report links in the message or rule `helpUri` instead.
+
+The default `-filter-mode=added` keeps diagnostics on added or modified lines.
+For a diagnostic that applies to a whole changed file, `-filter-mode=file` can be
+more appropriate. `-filter-mode=nofilter` helps inspect parsed diagnostics, but
+does not turn a non-file URI into a valid file path.
 
